            <div xml:id="d173">

                <pb facs="0327" n="215" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg215"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 4002/223–225.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Chargé Fletcher.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-08-12"><hi rendition="#italic">August 12,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 619.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 1198 of the 3d ultimo, regarding the municipal administration of places
                    along the line of the Chinese Eastern Railway, and inclosing a copy of the note
                    addressed to the Wai-wu Pu by you on June 23, 1909.</p>
                <p>The department has read your dispatch with interest and approves your note to the
                    Wai-wu Pu and the verbal statement which you report having made to the Russian
                    minister as to the objections of this Government to the new agreement.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
